  "stages": [
    {
      "stage": "A",
      "action": "Owner approves exact device and host read-only preflights. Obtain10MiB binary identities and allowlisted direct-entry inventory; hash private host config/key identities only with explicit new digest-only permission; bounded secret-presence checks emit booleans only.",
      "unknown_gate": "Any unknown/unowned entry, cap, process/actor mismatch or unexpected current service state blocks deletion or recovery; preserve and report, no repair."
    },
    {
      "stage": "B",
      "action": "After parent validates A, owner chooses proxy branch and separately renews saved/closed plus one new restart allowance. Selected recovery script stops only exact current transient client, parks only known owned adapter/liveQMD in prior approved rollback root, applies selected original-proxy disposition, requests restart once under CURRENT configuration, verifies service-byte fingerprints/current known activation unchanged and owned adapter/UIclient gone.",
      "not_done": "Parked code, config, CA/token copies and stages still exist. This is recovery/unmapping, not final cleanup."
    },
    {
      "stage": "C",
      "action": "Run selected frozen read-only verify and postinventory once under their explicit approvals after successful B. Re-enumerate exact experimental roots and known state-temp pattern after client quiescence. Collect actual identity/ownership/mtime of all final removal candidates; preserve state/history and originals.",
      "not_done": "A postinventory pass authorizes no deletion."
    },
    {
      "stage": "D",
      "action": "Build a NEW immutable exact deletion manifest from observed A/C facts. Each entry must carry absolute path, owner uid/gid, mode, type, size, mtime, exact allowed SHA256 or explicit opaque-preservation classification, root owner-marker provenance, and removal/preservation reason. Pin manifest SHA and exact deleting script bytes. Owner approves that exact irreversible scope before execution.",
      "real_missing_prerequisite": "Fresh A/C entry/identity facts, owner proxy choice and host gateway ownership/closure have not yet been obtained for this new proposal. Therefore no final deletion program or deletion manifest is represented as approved or complete now."
    },
    {
      "stage": "E-device",
      "action": "Recheck current service fingerprints, client inactive, owned adapter unmapped, no9821, selected original disposition, no unsafe/live actor, all parent/link/allowlist/hash guards BEFORE first deletion. Unlink ONLY approved exact known credential/config/CA/runtime-code files and known parked files. Never rm -r, wildcard-remove, reset state, delete unknown files or traverse notebook storage. Rmdir only explicitly approved directories proved empty; keep original state/temp/history/original-proxy roots as needed. On first mismatch stop; no silent repair or new restart.",
      "state_policy": "Keep /home/root/pi-ink-bridge-0020/state.json and numeric .tablet-state-* files in original owned root at0600, plus equivalent retained-root state if observed. No contents or state reset. Source diskState has association/terminal data rather than ServerConfig tokens.",
      "candidates": "Only exact known files from bounded fixed-path/entry inventory; roots and direct-child allowlists are embedded in frozen pre/postinventory. Unknown siblings are not candidates."
    },
    {
      "stage": "E-host",
      "action": "Resolve any current9443/9444 listener candidates to actual owned live origin sessions. Obtain exact closure authority; close only their actual gateway/request handles or separately approved exact process identity. Never revive stale jobs or kill shared OMP sessions from stale PIDs. Once endpoints are proved closed, re-pin and remove exact known config/token/key/runtime-payload copies under the audited /tmp roots and exact offline Go binary path. Preserve source/PDF/log/state/history boundaries.",
      "history_gate": "If bounded known-token/private-key-marker checks find credential material in retained logs, stop complete-cleanup claim. Obtain a separate precise preservation/redaction policy; never delete history silently. Unknown or oversized logs remain protected and block an exhaustive credential-copy claim."
    },
    {
      "stage": "F",
      "action": "Read-only bounded postproof verifies every approved removed file absent, all preserved opaque state metadata/original proxy metadata intact, no unknown deletion, service/settings fingerprints unchanged, owned runtime unmapped/inactive,9821 absent, host gateway listeners closed and approved credential/code copies absent. Record precise scoped completion and any preserved public source/evidence/history exceptions. Do not claim unsupported machine-wide erasure, original baseline restoration under quarantine choice, UI deployment or production acceptance."
    }
